From: radeon-custom rs480 reset-recovery track
Subject: [PATCH] drm/radeon: check every reset block on experimental RS480 masks via GUI_ACTIVE

Follow-up review fix for 0065 (PR #18). The 0065 mask-aware predicate checked
only RB3D_BUSY/RE_BUSY, so it missed PP (full_3d asserts S_0000F0_SOFT_RESET_PP)
and the CP reset that runs on every path.

Keep BASELINE -- and the discrete R3xx/R4xx path, which forces BASELINE --
exactly on the 0043 predicate (GA_BUSY || VAP_BUSY), so the non-experimental
path is unchanged. For a non-baseline (experimental) co-mask, additionally
require the master GUI_ACTIVE idle: one bit that catches every reset block,
including PP and the always-asserted CP, so a newly reset block left stuck is
not misread as recovered. This closes the PP/CP gaps without reintroducing the
0064 behaviour change on BASELINE/discrete.

No behaviour change on BASELINE or discrete R3xx/R4xx. No fire.

--- a/radeon/r300.c
+++ b/radeon/r300.c
@@ -593,16 +593,17 @@
 	/* restore PCI & busmastering */
 	pci_restore_state(rdev->pdev);
 	r100_enable_bm(rdev);
-	/* Check if GPU is idle, mask-aware.  GA and VAP are in every candidate and
-	 * are always checked (the 0043 baseline predicate).  RB3D and RE are checked
-	 * only when the asserted mask actually reset them, so a BASELINE reset -- and
-	 * the discrete R3xx/R4xx path, which forces BASELINE -- is classified exactly
-	 * as before and is never failed for a block it did not reset. */
+	/* Check if GPU is idle.  BASELINE -- and the discrete R3xx/R4xx path, which
+	 * forces BASELINE -- keeps exactly the 0043 predicate (GA_BUSY || VAP_BUSY):
+	 * no behaviour change on the non-experimental path.  An experimental co-mask
+	 * (GA_RB/GA_RE/full_3d) resets more blocks (RB3D, RE, and PP for full_3d), and
+	 * the CP reset below runs on every path, so for a non-baseline mask also
+	 * require the master GUI_ACTIVE idle -- one bit that catches every reset block
+	 * including PP and CP, so a newly reset block left stuck is not misread as
+	 * recovered. */
 	if (G_000E40_GA_BUSY(status) || G_000E40_VAP_BUSY(status) ||
-	    ((rs480_reset_used_mask & S_0000F0_SOFT_RESET_RB(1)) &&
-	     G_000E40_RB3D_BUSY(status)) ||
-	    ((rs480_reset_used_mask & S_0000F0_SOFT_RESET_RE(1)) &&
-	     G_000E40_RE_BUSY(status))) {
+	    (rs480_reset_used_mask != RS480_RESET_M_BASELINE &&
+	     G_000E40_GUI_ACTIVE(status))) {
 		dev_err(rdev->dev, "failed to reset GPU\n");
 		ret = -1;
 	} else
